==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!

Opening the case is a tricky task, as it is glued together. 
The recommended trick here, in order to avoid most damage potential to the plastic cover is:
USE A HEATGUN to warm up the outer border of the enclosure (~90ºC) and than start with a sharp knife to lift the cover step by step.
Insert a flat knife between the front and back casing below the ethernet port.
Open up a gap this way and insert a flat scredriver, remove the knife.

Work your way around the casing by applying force to seperate the front
and back casing. This losens the glue and opens the plastic clips. Be
gentle, as these clips are very cheap and break quickly.

